# Frontend conventions (bootloader — spec in `docs/frontend/conventions.md`)

Server-rendered Jinja2 + Bootstrap 5.3 + HTMX 1.9; no bundler, no SPA (ADR-001). Reuse before you invent.

## Must
- Pages `{% extends "base.html" %}`; exceptions are `viewer.html` and `markup.html` (fullscreen, own minimal helper copies — duplicate deliberately if they need a new shared helper).
- HTMX: target a specific `id`, return the matching `templates/partials/*.html`; hook post-swap work on `htmx:afterSwap`.
- Build version UIs from `OQB_VERSIONS` / `OQB_VERSION_LABELS` / `OQB_DEFAULT_VERSION_PRIORITY` (Jinja globals) — never a literal `EN/CH/BI` list. Version ordering UI = `oqbInitVersionPriorityWidget` (hidden comma input `version_priority`).
- Datetimes through `oqbFormatLocalTime` (`YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm`, 24 h); API values are naive-UTC ISO with `Z`.
- Drag-to-reorder uses **SortableJS** with the standard config (`forceFallback: true`, `delayOnTouchOnly`, `.drag-handle`, idempotent init via `container._sortableInstance`). Never native HTML5 DnD (breaks touch).
- Multi-select filters follow the custom Bootstrap dropdown + checkbox + hidden `<select multiple>` pattern.
- Gate admin UI on `window.OQB_IS_ADMIN` and AI UI on `window.OQB_AI_TOOLS_ENABLED` — cosmetic only; the server decorators are the gate.
- SSE consumers: `new EventSource(url)`, parse `{type, message, current, total}`, close on `type === 'done'`.
- New localStorage keys are prefixed `oqb_` and listed in `docs/frontend/conventions.md`.

## Shared pieces (do not re-implement)
- `base.html` helpers: `oqbTypesetMath`, `oqbRenderMarkdownInto`, `oqbLoadMarkdownPreviewCards`, `oqbPollDocThumbnails`, `oqbRerenderThumb`, `_oqbBuildThumbHtml`, `oqbParseUtc`, `oqbFormatLocalTime`.
- Partials: `question_list`, `edit_question_modal` + `edit_question_modal_js` (which already includes `tag_editor_js` — never include it twice), `tag_editor_form`, `md_editor`, `file_browser_{css,body,js}`, `file_selector` (`window.OQBFileSelector.open(...)`), `pdf_annotate_editor`, `_version_priority_widget_js`.
- Edit-modal host contract: set `window.oqbAfterQuestionEdit` and `window.oqbEditNavSource` on the host page (see `docs/modules/admin-questions.md`).
- Top-level `let`/`const` in a partial's script (e.g. `editQuestionData`) is **not** `window.<name>` — reading it that way is silently `undefined`. Reference it bare in the same file, or assign to `window.` explicitly when a host page must see it.
- Bounding-box overlays: mount `OQBBboxEditor` (`static/js/bbox_editor.js`). Host owns the item model; call `ed.restyle(item)` after mutating a box. Never reimplement a canvas painter. Spec: `docs/frontend/conventions.md` § Bounding-box editor.

## Gotchas
- `oqbPollDocThumbnails` must use the same cache-busted URL for probe and swap; per-element dedup via `data-doc-poller-active`.
- Keyboard shortcuts must be ignored while typing or when a stacked child modal is open.
- Reverse proxies need `proxy_buffering off` for SSE; nothing to do client-side.
- A new page needs a navbar entry in `base.html` and a row in `STATUS.md` frontend table.
